  "description": "Identity and subject-resolution add-on for Orleans.Lattice. Resolves a propagated caller credential into a LatticeSubject (a stable subject id plus its transitively expanded group closure) via a pluggable, IDP-independent authenticator seam (a JWT authenticator built in and designed to be specialized, plus an anonymous fallback), with configurable merging of token-asserted and directory groups. Backed by an introspectable group and membership-edge directory dogfooded onto reserved sys-membership-* Lattice trees with durable per-key history and per-silo resolution caching, and provides the identity-directory seam (a no-op default and a static roster built in) that admin surfaces use to search and validate principal ids. Enforces nothing on its own: authorization and enforcement come from Orleans.Lattice.Auth.",
